  "step_3": "The decision reason requires consideration of the differences between outcomes and a reference value (zero in this case), and a weighted evaluation of those differences (i.e., expected value), to determine which lottery has a more favorable mean difference. The individual, however, only considers the probability of winning (i.e., the chance of getting 4000 or 3000 Euros), without referencing any differences from a reference value or computing expected values. There is no mention of comparing differences, expected values, or the reference value. Therefore, the individual did not apply the decision reason. The reported reasoning is about preferring a higher probability of winning, which is a different criterion (e.g., risk preference or probability weighting), not the mean difference from a reference value. The two comparisons fail: (1) the relevant information (differences from reference, weighted by probabilities) is not considered by the individual; (2) the justification (preference for higher probability of winning) does not match the rule of the decision reason (which is based on expected value differences from a reference). Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
}

